@name Garnet triplet 50mm f/2
# Garnet triplet, 50 mm f/2: aspheric LuAG front element, polystyrene
# negative behind the stop, YAG rear element (Cooke triplet, stop between
# elements 1 and 2). All surfaces aspheric.
# Why: LuAG and YAG (cubic garnets, also as transparent ceramics) lie above
# the glass map: n 1.83-1.84 at V 52-58. With a low-index flint (polystyrene,
# n 1.59) the Petzval sum stays low. Material set X (catalogue without
# diamond). Polystyrene data: fit to Zhang et al. 2020; its partial
# dispersion is uncertain (README).
# Bar: 50 mm, 36 x 24, f/2, <= 3 elements, white-light RMS <= ~8 um at 0, 0.7, 1.0
# field, distortion <= 1 %, corner illumination >= 0.35, back focus >= 20 mm.
# Design: lens-render optimize (global search, equal budget for every material
# set): spherical screening of all glass combinations of each topology, then
# aspheric refinement of the best combinations, then 24 starts with one basin
# hop each (this job). Merit: RMS spot at 0, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.85, 1.0 field,
# 440/486/546/656 nm (0.5:1:2:1), object at infinity (1000 m); glass aspheres
# departure <= 0.5 mm. Experiment: lenses/novel/README.md.
# Numbers (lens-render numbers, f/2, infinity): RMS 5.0 / 10.0 / 9.0 um at
# 0 / 0.7 / 1.0 field (flat 440-660 nm: 5.8 / 9.5 / 10.3), distortion -0.29 %,
# corner illumination 0.39, length 75.3 mm, back focus 42.1 mm. At 2.5 m:
# 5.9 / 10.7 / 12.3 um. Misses the 8 um bar at 0.7 and 1.0 field.
#
# Generated by `lens-render optimize lenses/novel/garnet-triplet-f2.toml`.
# RMS spot (4 wavelengths) at f/2, object at 1000 m, by image height
# (fraction of 21.63 mm): 0: 6.1, 0.3: 7.0, 0.5: 8.8, 0.7: 9.8, 0.85: 8.7, 1: 10.1 µm. Units: mm.
#
# Global search: place 1, merit 4.3649e2 (start 16, seed 3).
#
